# DURABLE REPRO — D10 exclusivity hole A4: the read descends a FIELD PATH
# (`obj.data.get(0).unwrap()`) while the writer takes the whole owner (`&obj`).
#
# WRONG TODAY (measured at HEAD, Rust gg, C backend, `--sanitize`): `gg check`
# clean, then AddressSanitizer heap-use-after-free in `gorget_string_copy_cow`.
# The read's place is `obj.data[0]`, a strict sub-place of the writer's `obj`,
# so a place-overlap test on the resolved places catches it — but the syntactic
# check never resolves through the `.get()` view, so the two args look disjoint.
#
# INTENDED: REJECTED at `gg check` with `E_BorrowConflict`. (The prefix relation
# is the same one `d10b_place_overlap/writer_subfield_reject.gg` already pins
# for the non-view spelling.)
#
# The 4096-push loop FORCES a real reallocation.
#
#
# ORACLE (ggdef, measured this session): ACCEPTS this program and prints the
# pre-mutation value. ggdef is a definitional INTERPRETER with value semantics,
# so a reallocation cannot invalidate anything and this UAF class is
# structurally unobservable in that lane — it is NOT the authority here. The
# intended REJECT comes from the ratified D10 exclusivity ruling, which ggdef
# owes as part of the same landing (Core #9). Full note in
# `sound_excl_getchain_local.gg`.
# Cited from TODO.md (CoW / ownership / High): the D10 "one exclusive writer"
# structural-chokepoint entry, hole #1 (field-path costume).
struct Bag:
    Vector[String] data

void f(String s, Bag &b):
    int i = 0
    while i < 4096:
        b.data.push("filler-padding-to-force-a-real-reallocation")
        i = i + 1
    print(s)

void main():
    Bag obj = Bag(Vector[String]())
    obj.data.push("alpha-heap-forced-payload")
    f(obj.data.get(0).unwrap(), &obj)
